<BaseLayout title="About — doon.today" description="What doon.today is, and how to report a mistake or a missing event.">
  <section class="simple-page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT</p>
    <h1>A calendar for Doon.</h1>
    <p class="about-callout">We now have a <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>: see what's new on the site.</p>
    <p>Doon.today collects public event information from ticketing platforms, organizers and local community sources, then filters it for Dehradun relevance.</p>
    <p>The project is intentionally text-first and calendar-first. It is not a ticket marketplace and does not require an account.</p>
    <p>Events come one of two ways. Those tagged with a group’s handle (or “Community”) were posted by Dehradun’s own clubs and groups, or sent in through the form, and were checked by hand. The rest are taken from listing sites such as District and AllEvents and refreshed three times a day. Each event page says which, and when it was last checked.</p>

    <h2>Spot a mistake, or a missing event?</h2>
    <p>Every event page has a <strong>Report a problem</strong> link, and <strong>Feedback</strong> at the bottom of every page opens a short form; messages come straight to us and are never made public. To add an event we have missed, use <strong>Submit Event</strong> at the top of the page; every entry is checked by hand before it is published.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
